WEBVTT

00:00.520 --> 00:10.780
Tsuki no kaasu tsumetai yume no naka de

00:00.520 --> 00:10.780
Under the moon’s curse, inside of a cold dream…

00:19.160 --> 00:25.540
Kotoba no nai sekai de bokura wa ai wo kataru

00:19.160 --> 00:25.540
In a world without words, we speak of love

00:25.540 --> 00:29.750
itsuka kimi ni todoku made

00:25.540 --> 00:29.750
until it reaches you someday.

00:32.340 --> 00:39.220
Kizu darake no kaina de dakiyoseta kuchibiru no

00:32.340 --> 00:39.220
I want to melt the frozen over wish...

00:39.220 --> 00:45.060
haritsumeta negai tokashitakute

00:39.220 --> 00:45.060
from the lips that I embraced with arms covered in wounds.

00:45.140 --> 00:51.860
Nee, aishiatta kako no utsukushisa sutesareba

00:45.140 --> 00:51.860
Hey, if I abandon the beauty of the past when we loved each other,

00:52.240 --> 00:58.030
ashita motto kirei na yoru e yukeru kara

00:52.240 --> 00:58.030
then tomorrow, I can go to a more beautiful night.

00:58.410 --> 01:06.620
Tsuki no kaasu tsumetai yume no naka kara

00:58.410 --> 01:06.620
Under the moon’s curse, from inside of a cold dream.

01:06.620 --> 01:12.800
Kimi wo tooku tsuresaritakute

01:06.620 --> 01:12.800
I want to take you somewhere far away,

01:13.340 --> 01:16.680
doko made yukeru

01:13.340 --> 01:16.680
and go anywhere,

01:16.680 --> 01:24.890
ai wo shinjite ii basho made

01:16.680 --> 01:24.890
to a place where we can believe in love.

01:32.990 --> 01:34.300
Seimei...

01:35.070 --> 01:38.190
Where are you now?

01:39.410 --> 01:42.410
Mom says death is the end.

01:42.410 --> 01:44.750
Once you die, everything ends.

01:48.840 --> 01:50.500
I don't know...

01:51.260 --> 01:53.390
Seimei definitely was "here"...

01:54.050 --> 01:57.830
I remember his voice, his warmth...

02:03.560 --> 02:06.600
What were you praying
about for that long?

02:07.370 --> 02:08.440
Nothing.

02:09.300 --> 02:10.100
Tell me...

02:11.150 --> 02:12.940
I'd love to make it happen.

02:15.870 --> 02:18.160
You want me to tell you?

02:18.160 --> 02:19.410
I prayed for two things.

02:19.990 --> 02:23.000
One is to remember what I
was like until two years ago...

02:23.370 --> 02:27.370
The other is something
you can do if you want to...

02:27.370 --> 02:31.720
I want to know about the Septimal
Moon, the people who killed Seimei...

02:31.720 --> 02:33.920
Ritsuka, I can't do that.

02:34.670 --> 02:36.390
I thought so!

02:36.390 --> 02:37.970
You're that kind of guy!

02:38.600 --> 02:40.550
You say pretty things...

02:41.850 --> 02:43.350
...but you don't mean it!

02:43.890 --> 02:46.960
I'll do anything besides that, really.

02:47.730 --> 02:49.100
Please command me.

02:49.440 --> 02:50.880
Oh really!

02:50.880 --> 02:52.880
You're really going
to do anything, right?

02:54.700 --> 02:55.820
If I tell you to die...

02:56.660 --> 02:57.280
Okay.

02:57.280 --> 02:58.720
Fine then!

02:58.720 --> 03:00.450
Do you know the Iriomote cat?

03:01.240 --> 03:02.420
Iriomote...

03:02.420 --> 03:04.740
I learned about it in school...

03:04.740 --> 03:07.910
It's a wild cat from Iriomote island in
Okinawa, protected by the government.

03:08.540 --> 03:10.180
I'll capture it.

03:10.180 --> 03:13.130
No! It's an endangered animal!

03:13.130 --> 03:16.300
A picture! Go find
it and take a picture!

03:17.220 --> 03:18.220
Okay.

03:18.220 --> 03:19.590
"Okay"?

03:19.830 --> 03:21.720
Don't think it's easy!

03:21.720 --> 03:23.930
It's impossible to find an Iriomote cat!

03:25.020 --> 03:27.640
For you, I can.

03:29.730 --> 03:31.210
Whatever!

03:31.210 --> 03:33.280
You're just all talk...

03:33.280 --> 03:35.650
I can't believe people like that!

03:41.490 --> 03:44.380
Soubi, you really like butterflies.

03:44.380 --> 03:45.510
Butterflies?

03:45.510 --> 03:46.730
I despise them.

03:47.390 --> 03:48.330
You hate them?

03:48.750 --> 03:50.600
I hate the fact that it's pretty...

03:50.600 --> 03:53.160
...easy to capture...

03:53.160 --> 03:57.590
...and above all, for having a pin stuck
in its body for use as a specimen.

03:58.090 --> 03:59.630
What's with you?

03:59.970 --> 04:01.470
That's not the butterflies' fault.

04:03.930 --> 04:06.540
Those ears, who pierced it for you?

04:06.540 --> 04:07.670
Ritsuka.

04:09.090 --> 04:10.810
That brat in the picture?

04:10.810 --> 04:14.400
Don't make him do that. Poor kid.

04:14.400 --> 04:16.190
You're such a pervert.

04:16.190 --> 04:18.730
Kio, I'm not a pervert.

04:19.810 --> 04:22.530
So, are you really okay about tonight?

04:23.420 --> 04:24.110
Yes.

04:25.040 --> 04:27.440
There's only one bed, right?

04:27.440 --> 04:30.330
Yes, you can use it. I'll be out.

04:30.330 --> 04:33.610
W-What do you mean you'll be out?

04:33.610 --> 04:34.540
Where are you going?

04:36.170 --> 04:37.460
It's a secret.

04:38.930 --> 04:40.380
Soubi!

04:42.600 --> 04:44.690
Good morning, Seimei...

04:50.750 --> 04:51.350
Mom!

05:10.480 --> 05:13.000
I wonder what happened to Ritsuka...

05:13.000 --> 05:15.580
It's already noon and he's not here...

05:19.500 --> 05:21.040
Strawberry pickings?

05:21.040 --> 05:21.840
At this season?

05:22.100 --> 05:25.630
Uh-huh. We were really
gonna go this past spring...

05:26.140 --> 05:30.230
...but Dad got busy at work and
we finally went two days ago.

05:30.230 --> 05:31.600
Our whole family!

05:32.350 --> 05:35.390
This place has strawberry picking all year long.

05:35.940 --> 05:37.190
Greenhouse horticulture, huh?

05:37.580 --> 05:39.450
It was delicious!

05:39.450 --> 05:43.570
But it's impossible to eat
bunches of strawberries.

05:44.160 --> 05:46.830
I wanted to eat a
hundred, but I couldn't.

05:47.540 --> 05:50.830
So we made jam at home.

05:51.870 --> 05:52.740
Jam?

05:53.290 --> 05:55.650
I promised yesterday...

05:56.340 --> 05:58.000
Ooh, naughty!

05:58.950 --> 06:01.110
What did you bring to school?

06:02.460 --> 06:05.620
What's this? It has a spooky color.

06:05.620 --> 06:06.760
Give it back!

06:06.760 --> 06:08.740
So what is this?

06:09.100 --> 06:10.250
Strawberry...

06:10.250 --> 06:11.510
Strawberry jam.

06:11.510 --> 06:12.470
No way!

06:12.470 --> 06:13.380
I'm serious!

06:13.380 --> 06:15.230
I made it with my mom!

06:15.980 --> 06:17.520
Yuiko's homemade jam?

06:19.400 --> 06:25.030
H-Homemade means Yuiko was touching
it with her finger and licking it...

06:26.450 --> 06:27.950
I-I want to eat...

06:27.950 --> 06:30.750
...Yuiko, I mean, her homemade jam...

06:31.290 --> 06:32.820
Please give it back.

06:33.920 --> 06:35.190
No way!

06:35.190 --> 06:39.250
You're not allowed to bring
thing like this to school.

06:39.250 --> 06:41.630
Hey, hand that to me!

06:41.630 --> 06:42.510
Come on!

06:44.120 --> 06:47.300
Y-Yuiko, can I taste
a little of this jam?

06:47.300 --> 06:49.060
Um, but...

06:49.060 --> 06:50.680
No, you can't!

06:51.070 --> 06:52.620
Hey, hand it back to me!

06:53.510 --> 06:54.890
No way!

06:54.890 --> 06:57.270
Just one, just one lick!

06:57.270 --> 07:00.810
No! I promised yesterday!
It's for Ritsuka!

07:01.180 --> 07:01.980
Ritsuka?

07:17.960 --> 07:20.370
U-Um, Yuiko...

07:23.500 --> 07:26.160
Why are you crying?

07:26.160 --> 07:28.300
You're the one who brought it to school.

07:28.300 --> 07:30.010
It's your fault.

07:30.010 --> 07:31.180
That's right.

07:31.180 --> 07:32.470
Such a drag.

07:32.470 --> 07:36.280
Hawatari, what are you trying
to do, creating all this ruckus?

07:36.280 --> 07:38.100
Apologize to everybody!

07:38.100 --> 07:39.850
Yeah, apologize!

07:39.850 --> 07:40.940
Don't be crying!

07:40.940 --> 07:42.060
Apologize to everybody!

07:42.060 --> 07:43.520
Mommy!

07:50.030 --> 07:50.860
Aoyagi...

07:56.330 --> 07:57.910
Hmm delicious.

08:00.080 --> 08:02.500
You guys are pitiful!

08:03.170 --> 08:05.010
Are you even human?

08:05.010 --> 08:11.470
Yuiko worked real hard to make it, and
then she brought it to school, that's it.

08:12.220 --> 08:13.310
W-What?

08:13.310 --> 08:15.350
That's what she's not allowed to do!

08:15.350 --> 08:16.310
Yeah!

08:16.310 --> 08:18.890
And besides, Yayoi is
the one who dropped it!

08:20.060 --> 08:21.950
It might be Yayoi who
broke the container...

08:21.950 --> 08:26.020
...and made it impossible to eat the
jam that Yuiko worked hard to make.

08:27.190 --> 08:31.140
But you guys are the ones
who hurt her feelings!

08:31.140 --> 08:35.070
It's worse than breaking
things, and breaking rules!

08:35.070 --> 08:36.820
You guys should all...

08:37.450 --> 08:38.680
just die!

08:42.200 --> 08:43.450
Aoyagi!

08:43.450 --> 08:46.210
Don't say words like
that to your friends.

08:48.420 --> 08:50.190
And you girls too!

08:50.190 --> 08:51.880
You should keep it down.

08:52.180 --> 08:55.220
And Hawatari, you should be careful too.

08:55.220 --> 08:56.260
Understand?

08:56.760 --> 08:57.340
Teacher...

08:58.060 --> 09:02.020
I think it's worse to hurt someone's
feelings than to hurt them physically.

09:05.070 --> 09:08.240
Aoyagi, you have a lot of
bruises. What's going on?

09:08.240 --> 09:08.770
Nothing...

09:09.570 --> 09:13.570
I'm clumsy, so I often
trip and bump into things...

09:14.580 --> 09:16.290
That's all.

09:22.670 --> 09:24.000
Oh, no!

09:24.000 --> 09:26.800
I was called by our
teacher about the incident.

09:26.800 --> 09:29.350
She told me to come by after school.

09:29.350 --> 09:30.800
I'm gonna go real quick!

09:30.800 --> 09:31.930
Wait for me!

09:32.960 --> 09:34.260
(Sign: Student Guidance Room)

09:35.100 --> 09:37.930
I see. I understand the situation.

09:38.930 --> 09:40.680
By the way, Hawatari...

09:41.030 --> 09:42.000
Yes?

09:42.520 --> 09:46.640
What kind of person is Aoyagi,
from your point of view?

09:47.470 --> 09:49.600
Ritsuka?

09:49.600 --> 09:50.410
Yes...

09:52.150 --> 09:53.860
Teacher, please hear me out!

09:54.130 --> 09:56.030
Uh, okay...

09:56.300 --> 09:58.660
I... I love Ritsuka!

09:58.660 --> 09:59.430
What?

10:00.580 --> 10:03.680
When he came to our class,
I thought he was really cool...

10:03.680 --> 10:06.310
I wanted to be friends.

10:07.800 --> 10:13.130
He stands up for me. He protects me.

10:13.800 --> 10:15.830
After today, I like him even more...

10:16.430 --> 10:20.770
I want to do anything for
him, but I don't know what to do.

10:21.520 --> 10:26.430
I will do anything for
Ritsuka. I would even die for him!

10:35.990 --> 10:38.240
I understand your feelings.

10:40.410 --> 10:43.760
But don't say that
you'll "die" for someone.

10:44.170 --> 10:49.540
You meet people you like through your
life, and you are able to feel love.

10:50.460 --> 10:53.300
Once you die, everything's over...

10:54.180 --> 10:56.650
Think more about the importance of life.

10:57.510 --> 10:58.300
Understand?

10:59.930 --> 11:00.970
Yes...

11:03.160 --> 11:05.150
Y-Yuiko...

11:05.640 --> 11:09.480
You like Ritsuka Aoyagi that much...

11:11.150 --> 11:12.940
But I still love you!

11:24.740 --> 11:25.950
Hey, Loveless.

11:28.830 --> 11:30.070
Ritsuka Aoyagi...

11:31.500 --> 11:33.460
Hmm, you don't look so good.

11:35.260 --> 11:36.750
Hey, look over here!

11:37.020 --> 11:40.130
We're in front of school.
Keep your voices down.

11:40.130 --> 11:42.510
Come with us. We have to talk.

11:42.850 --> 11:43.680
Talk?

11:47.390 --> 11:50.610
Don't be scared. We're not going
to attack you all of a sudden.

12:09.880 --> 12:12.290
I would die for him, huh...

12:13.420 --> 12:14.710
I'm envious...

12:14.960 --> 12:17.920
Yanjounan Primary School

12:14.960 --> 12:17.920
Ritsuka Aoyagi

12:14.960 --> 12:17.920
Documentation

12:27.060 --> 12:35.060
The phone number you have called is
currently out of range or turned off.

12:36.360 --> 12:37.900
Call me anytime.

12:38.220 --> 12:39.860
I'll always answer it.

12:41.660 --> 12:43.600
Soubi!, that jerk!

12:44.200 --> 12:46.120
Sorry, did I keep you waiting?

12:48.410 --> 12:49.800
Ritsuka...

12:52.960 --> 12:53.890
Yuiko...

12:56.570 --> 12:57.900
Oh, Yayoi...

12:59.340 --> 13:03.690
If you're looking for Aoyagi, he
was taken by two strange people.

13:04.890 --> 13:06.370
Two strange people?

13:06.370 --> 13:08.050
Maybe from before...

13:08.460 --> 13:11.560
Which way? Which way did they go?

13:12.150 --> 13:13.100
Huh? Um...

13:13.100 --> 13:14.440
That way, okay!

13:15.240 --> 13:17.350
Y-Yeah, Yuiko...

13:20.990 --> 13:23.320
We're gonna do it here?

13:23.870 --> 13:24.730
Do what?

13:24.730 --> 13:25.970
Sorry for the wait.

13:27.790 --> 13:28.930
Here, Ai.

13:29.460 --> 13:30.120
Here.

13:31.460 --> 13:33.410
It's not poisoned.

13:33.790 --> 13:37.420
Mango green tea frappuccino
with caramel flavor.

13:37.420 --> 13:39.210
A limited time special drink!

13:39.920 --> 13:41.740
There's no reason for you to treat me.

13:42.530 --> 13:44.010
That's not cute...

13:46.350 --> 13:47.590
Yum, good.

13:48.070 --> 13:49.500
So we're not going to fight?

13:49.500 --> 13:52.100
Can you fight on your own, eh?

13:54.010 --> 13:56.020
Just came to say hi.

13:56.020 --> 13:56.620
Huh?

13:57.230 --> 14:00.360
We've been taken off the mission.

14:00.360 --> 14:02.640
We're not gonna fight with you anymore...

14:02.640 --> 14:05.610
If it's not a mission, we
have no grudge against you.

14:05.610 --> 14:08.320
We're being sent back to school.

14:08.990 --> 14:10.020
School?

14:10.580 --> 14:12.910
There's a school at the Septimal Moon?

14:13.150 --> 14:16.150
You really don't know anything, huh?

14:16.540 --> 14:18.150
It's school for Sentouki.

14:18.550 --> 14:20.150
Sentouki...

14:20.150 --> 14:21.860
Soubi was there too.

14:23.250 --> 14:25.670
Don't get fooled.

14:25.670 --> 14:27.550
He's the worst.

14:27.820 --> 14:29.980
Then who are you guys?

14:29.980 --> 14:31.840
Can you tell me the truth?

14:31.840 --> 14:34.520
What did you do to Seimei? Tell me!

14:38.020 --> 14:39.140
We can't.

14:39.730 --> 14:44.450
But if you split up with
Soubi and come with us...

14:44.910 --> 14:48.940
...the teacher will tell you everything.

14:48.940 --> 14:50.070
Everything?

14:50.790 --> 14:54.540
You should split up
with that lying adult!

14:59.460 --> 15:02.920
He is certainly a liar.

15:03.800 --> 15:05.120
I know that...

15:05.590 --> 15:10.100
...but splitting up and whatever else
will be decided between Soubi and me!

15:10.720 --> 15:12.340
I won't be dictated to!

15:14.730 --> 15:16.260
Fine, then.

15:16.260 --> 15:22.400
Anyway there will be somebody
who will be deployed to kidnap you.

15:33.910 --> 15:34.910
Ritsuka!

15:36.960 --> 15:37.660
Yuiko.

15:43.130 --> 15:44.540
Ritsuka, are you okay?

15:44.760 --> 15:45.420
Huh?

15:46.130 --> 15:48.730
Those people, who are they?

15:48.730 --> 15:51.050
Didn't they come to bully you?

15:51.470 --> 15:53.150
It's nothing like that...

15:53.150 --> 15:53.800
Wanna drink this?

15:54.930 --> 15:56.830
Wow, thanks!

15:58.560 --> 16:01.480
My goodness! This is really good!

16:08.200 --> 16:11.530
Yuiko and Aoyagi!

16:11.740 --> 16:13.710
I will never give up...

16:13.710 --> 16:17.070
Someday, my feelings will reach Yuiko!

16:17.410 --> 16:19.410
Because, Yuiko...

16:20.000 --> 16:23.450
I would die for you, too!

16:31.350 --> 16:33.720
According to the last school's reports...

16:33.720 --> 16:38.260
...Aoyagi's grades weren't too
great, but he was popular in class.

16:39.140 --> 16:43.770
But after his tenth birthday, during
the third semester of fourth grade...

16:43.770 --> 16:45.870
...he became the exact opposite.

16:46.490 --> 16:47.230
Two years ago...

16:48.200 --> 16:50.380
What happened two years ago?

16:50.910 --> 16:55.250
Even though these things can happen during a child's development, but...

16:55.250 --> 16:58.440
...in any case, I must
meet with the parents.

17:03.040 --> 17:05.420
I... I love Ritsuka!

17:06.090 --> 17:07.250
I would die for him!

17:13.350 --> 17:18.030
I wonder if I can find somebody
who makes me feel like that...

17:24.010 --> 17:26.770
Littering cigarette butts
in a place like this!

17:33.030 --> 17:34.030
Agatsuma?

17:38.040 --> 17:38.660
Yes?

17:39.110 --> 17:41.040
U-Um...

17:41.040 --> 17:41.950
You are?

17:43.160 --> 17:44.120
Aoyagi

17:45.210 --> 17:47.440
Aoyagi's teacher...

17:47.440 --> 17:49.960
Today, um, I'm about to visit his home...

17:50.320 --> 17:51.620
House call?

17:52.720 --> 17:53.920
Ritsuka's teacher?

17:53.920 --> 17:54.660
Yes.

17:56.100 --> 17:57.530
You know about me?

17:57.530 --> 17:58.500
Yes...

17:58.500 --> 18:03.350
Well, when you were at the
back gate, Aoyagi told me...

18:05.020 --> 18:07.310
...that you're a friend of his brother.

18:07.860 --> 18:09.470
Ritsuka talked about me...

18:14.950 --> 18:15.530
Teacher!

18:15.530 --> 18:17.100
Y-Yes!

18:17.930 --> 18:19.320
How old are you?

18:20.450 --> 18:21.800
W-What? How old?

18:22.290 --> 18:25.620
Me? Um, I'm 23...

18:25.910 --> 18:27.080
23!

18:28.030 --> 18:29.580
Pretty up there...

18:30.050 --> 18:32.340
I'm not interested in older people.

18:32.600 --> 18:33.240
What?

18:35.470 --> 18:36.730
Soubi!

18:37.680 --> 18:40.800
What are you saying to
my teacher? I heard you!

18:41.120 --> 18:44.250
Well, it'll be annoying
if she starts liking me...

18:45.310 --> 18:46.690
...so I nipped it in the bud.

18:47.650 --> 18:50.270
That's not possible.

18:51.110 --> 18:52.080
Really?

18:52.080 --> 18:53.980
Then please don't cry.

18:55.450 --> 18:57.570
Teacher, are you okay?

18:57.570 --> 18:59.030
Soubi, apologize!

19:00.660 --> 19:02.370
I'm sorry.

19:05.700 --> 19:07.340
Teacher!

19:07.340 --> 19:08.480
She's left.

19:09.540 --> 19:11.420
What are you doing?

19:11.420 --> 19:13.390
Why are you making my teacher cry?

19:13.760 --> 19:15.210
What do you mean why?

19:15.680 --> 19:17.720
It'd be an annoyance if
that kind of person liked me.

19:17.720 --> 19:18.550
Soubi!

19:19.700 --> 19:20.680
Upset?

19:22.230 --> 19:25.010
Then give me corporal punishment.

19:29.190 --> 19:29.980
I...

19:31.150 --> 19:32.940
I won't hit anyone.

19:34.530 --> 19:36.610
I won't use violence!

19:37.080 --> 19:40.180
This is discipline more than violence.

19:40.180 --> 19:41.800
No means no!

19:43.450 --> 19:44.240
Okay, okay.

19:45.750 --> 19:49.460
Anyway, why was my teacher here?

19:49.460 --> 19:50.330
Not sure.

19:51.710 --> 19:52.830
What about you?

19:54.590 --> 19:56.290
I wanted to see Ritsuka.

19:56.880 --> 19:58.840
Then why didn't you answer the phone?

19:59.550 --> 20:01.510
You said you'd answer anytime.

20:02.430 --> 20:05.010
But, you called?

20:05.980 --> 20:07.080
Anything happened?

20:07.520 --> 20:08.620
Nothing.

20:09.230 --> 20:12.730
Sorry, I was at a place
where there was no signal.

20:13.400 --> 20:15.590
You really are the lowest of the low!

20:16.360 --> 20:19.530
You make my teacher cry and you lie!

20:20.990 --> 20:22.100
Sorry...

20:22.100 --> 20:23.990
Hey, look at this.

20:30.630 --> 20:31.410
What is this?

20:32.210 --> 20:33.710
No! No way!

20:34.250 --> 20:37.380
See, the fat tail is
one of its characteristics.

20:37.880 --> 20:40.830
So, the place where the
signal didn't reach was...

20:41.370 --> 20:44.840
B-But, this cat rarely shows
itself in front of people...

20:48.250 --> 20:51.920
I told you. I'll do
anything if it's for Ritsuka.

20:52.440 --> 20:54.060
There's nothing I can't do.

20:55.280 --> 20:56.530
Soubi.

21:08.790 --> 21:11.730
My life belongs to Ritsuka...

21:12.130 --> 21:15.450
For Ritsuka, I'll die anytime.

21:16.800 --> 21:20.400
Don't say it too lightly!

21:23.470 --> 21:26.590
But it's true...

21:27.220 --> 21:32.180
To be continued...

21:28.970 --> 21:38.520
Setsunasa no kagiri made dakishimete mo

21:28.970 --> 21:38.520
Even if I hold you with all my suffering,

21:39.310 --> 21:48.820
itsu made mo hitotsu ni wa narenakute

21:39.310 --> 21:48.820
we still can't be one.

21:49.410 --> 21:59.330
Yasashisa yori fukai basho de fureau no wa itami dake

21:49.410 --> 21:59.330
The only thing that we can feel deep within besides kindness is pain,

21:59.750 --> 22:07.340
futari wo musunde kudasai

21:59.750 --> 22:07.340
so please, bind the two of us together.

22:09.890 --> 22:14.720
Bokura wa mou yume wo minai

22:09.890 --> 22:14.720
We no longer dream anymore,

22:14.720 --> 22:19.860
tomadoinagara te wo totte

22:14.720 --> 22:19.860
when you're wavering, take my hand

22:20.150 --> 22:29.070
zankoku na yoake no hou e arukidasu

22:20.150 --> 22:29.070
as we tread towards the cruel light of dawn.

22:30.200 --> 22:40.210
Hontou no kotoba wa kitto hontou no sekai no dokoka

22:30.200 --> 22:40.210
I'm sure real words are somewhere in the real world.

22:40.540 --> 22:49.430
Bokura no mukuchi na yoru ni hisonderu

22:40.540 --> 22:49.430
They lurk in the shadows of our silent nights.

22:49.800 --> 22:54.930
Ima mo kitto

22:49.800 --> 22:54.930
Surely, even now...

23:01.600 --> 23:03.820
The enemy's name is Sleepless.

23:04.400 --> 23:06.140
The night that does not sleep.

23:06.140 --> 23:10.320
The memo they have has
something I want to know.

23:10.700 --> 23:12.330
Soubi, get it!

23:12.660 --> 23:14.340
Yes, master.

23:15.580 --> 23:17.920
Tale five, Sleepless.

23:19.540 --> 23:23.850
Between Ritsuka and I, this
universe's rules have been annihilated.
